{"id": "EUVD-2026-102339", "enisaUuid": "4e283fef-7757-360b-89e6-3b1198e21749", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains a CRLF injection vulnerability in services_unbound_acls.php that allows authenticated users with the DNS Resolver: Access Lists privilege to inject Unbound configuration directives. Attackers can embed CR/LF characters in the aclname or aclaction fields written to access_lists.conf to add local-data, local-zone, or forward-zone directives and control DNS answers served to LAN clients.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:10:35", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:L/SA:L", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-unbound-acl-crlf", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/unbound.inc#L1094-L1112", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/services_unbound_acls.php#L121-L142", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-crlf-injection-via-services-unbound-acls-php"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4m9r-jxrh-x66q", "CVE-2026-111227"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.84, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "85d6c6bf-93ba-389f-ad57-92c30fb8de80", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5c8c12c0-23fd-374d-a653-2e0e3ba70621", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}